## About Swedish law

Swedish legislation consists of acts adopted by the Riksdag, ordinances decided by the Government, and regulations issued by agencies under delegated authority, such as Elsäkerhetsverket, Arbetsmiljöverket and MSB.

## Role in the regulatory landscape

Swedish regulations are often transpositions of EU law or international conventions. Agencies issue binding regulations (for example ELSÄK-FS, AFS and MSBFS) as well as general guidelines.
